Change the administrator password through the local control socket.

Read one password from a protected file or pipe on stdin. It needs at least
12 characters. --no-password removes it. Every browser session is revoked.
The API token is separate and is not changed.

Usage:
  olr system set password [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help          help for password
      --no-password   remove the password; anyone who can reach this router may configure it
      --password      set the password from redirected stdin (the default)

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
